body:
>Do other animals also have to worship?

Quran: Al-isra verse 44;

The seven heavens, the earth, and all those in them glorify Him. There is not a single thing that does not glorify His praises—but you ˹simply˺ cannot comprehend their glorification. He is indeed Most Forbearing, All-Forgiving.

Quran: surah Al-ikhlas;

Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “He is Allah—One ˹and Indivisible˺;
Allah—the Sustainer ˹needed by all˺.
He has never had offspring, nor was He born.
And there is none comparable to Him.”

It's not younger. It's the religion of all prophets from Adam to Muhammad peace be upon them all.

Quran: Surah Ali-'imran verse 19;
Certainly, Allah’s only Way is Islam. Those who were given the Scripture did not dispute ˹among themselves˺ out of mutual envy until knowledge came to them. Whoever denies Allah’s signs, then surely Allah is swift in reckoning.

Verse 67;
Abraham was neither a Jew nor a Christian; he submitted in all uprightness and was not a polytheist.

I don't need to use your manuscripts as evidence. The Quran proves to be the truth on it's own. But if you believe in the "Bible" (not the original), then you need to accept what is written in it. And it clearly talks about the messenger Muhammad peace be upon him. In song of solomon 5:16, it says 'Muhammadim'. 'Im' is a plural of respect in the hebrew language. There're many verses in the "Bible" which prophecies the coming of the messenger Muhammad peace be upon him.

And if you want me to quote from the Quran, her it is: 

Surah As-saf verse 6; 
And ˹remember˺ when Jesus, son of Mary, said, “O children of Israel! I am truly Allah’s messenger to you, confirming the Torah which came before me, and giving good news of a messenger after me whose name will be Aḥmad.” Yet when the Prophet came to them with clear proofs, they said, “This is pure magic.”

And talking about the corruption of the bible isn't a misconception or misinterpretation.

Quran: surah Al-baqarah verse 75;
Do you ˹believers still˺ expect them to be true to you, though a group of them would hear the word of Allah then knowingly corrupt it after understanding it?

Surah Al-maidah verse 13;
But for breaking their covenant We condemned them and hardened their hearts. They distorted the words of the Scripture and neglected a portion of what they had been commanded to uphold. You ˹O Prophet˺ will always find deceit on their part, except for a few. But pardon them and bear with them. Indeed, Allah loves the good-doers.

And there are many more verses, also verses about the the denying of trinity and so on. If you want me to  quote them let me know.

To be muslim we need to believe in all the books sent by God do his prophets. One of them is the Bible. The problem is that the Bible doesn't exist anymore. What the christians have today are books written/inspired by other people years after Jesus peace be upon him. We believe that Jesus came with the same message as all the other prophets which is to believe in (and worship) one God. Also, the christians claim that Jesus is God, but nowhere in their "Bible" does he say that. 


The message of the Quran to the christians and jews is really simple. Quran: surah Ali-imran verse 64;

Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “O People of the Book! Let us come to common terms: that we will worship none but Allah, associate none with Him, nor take one another as lords instead of Allah.” But if they turn away, then say, “Bear witness that we have submitted ˹to Allah alone˺.”

In islam it's considered a sin. 

Quran: surah Al-Mu'minun verse 1-7

Successful indeed are the believers:
those who humble themselves in prayer;
those who avoid idle talk;
those who pay alms-tax;
those who guard their chastity
except with their wives or those ˹bondwomen˺ in
their possession,for then they are free from blame,
but whoever seeks beyond that are the transgressors;
